      "direction_name": "Agent Skills 与 Harness",
      "week": "2026-W25",
      "title": "TaPERA: Enhancing Faithfulness and Interpretability in Long-Form Table QA by Content Planning and Execution-based Reasoning",
      "title_zh": "TaPERA：基于内容规划与执行式推理提升长文本表格问答的忠实性与可解释性",
      "authors": [
        "Yilun Zhao",
        "Lyuhao Chen",
        "Arman Cohan",
        "Chen Zhao"
      ],
      "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/98061d19d69ed3089d1ee5558e0d650cb1e253a8",
      "pdf_url": "",
      "category": "via-citation",
      "published": "",
      "collected": "2026-06-15",
      "abstract": "Long-form Table Question Answering (L F TQA) requires systems to generate para-graph long and complex answers to questions over tabular data. While Large language models based systems have made significant progress, it often hallucinates, especially when the task involves complex reasoning over tables. To tackle this issue, we propose a new LLM-based framework, T A PERA, for L F TQA tasks. Our framework uses a modular approach that decomposes the whole process into three sub-modules: 1) QA-based Content Planner that iteratively decomposes the input question into sub-questions; 2) Execution-based Table Reasoner that produces executable Python program for each sub-question; and 3) Answer Generator that generates long-form answer grounded on the program output. Human evaluation results on the F E T A QA and QTS UMM datasets indicate that our framework significantly improves strong baselines on both accuracy and truthfulness, as our modular framework is better at table reasoning, and the long-form answer is always consistent with the program output. Our modular design further provides transparency as users are able to interact with our framework by manually changing the content plans.",
      "abstract_zh": "长文本表格问答需要系统针对表格数据生成段落级长复杂回答，现有基于大语言模型的方法虽有进展，但在复杂表格推理时常产生幻觉。为此本文提出模块化框架TaPERA，将流程分为内容规划、执行推理、答案生成三个子模块，在两个公开数据集的人工评测中显著提升了基线性能。",
