      "id": "2606.14832",
      "direction_id": "agent-skills-harness",
      "direction_name": "Agent Skills 与 Harness",
      "week": "2026-W25",
      "title": "PhoneHarness: Harnessing Phone-Use Agents through Mixed GUI, CLI, and Tool Actions",
      "title_zh": "PhoneHarness：通过混合GUI、CLI与工具动作驾驭手机使用智能体",
      "authors": [
        "Chenxin Li",
        "Zhengyao Fang",
        "Zhengyang Tang",
        "Pengyuan Lyu",
        "Xingran Zhou",
        "X. Lai",
        "Fei Tang",
        "Liang Wu",
        "Yiduo Guo",
        "Weinong Wang",
        "Junyi Li",
        "Yi Zhang",
        "Yang Ding",
        "Huawen Shen",
        "Sunqi Fan",
        "Shangpin Peng",
        "Zhenghao Ruan",
        "Anran Zhang",
        "Benyou Wang",
        "Chengquan Zhang",
        "Han Hu"
      ],
      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2606.14832",
      "pdf_url": "http://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.14832",
      "category": "via-citation",
      "published": "",
      "collected": "2026-06-17",
      "abstract": "Phone agents are increasingly expected to complete real mobile workflows rather than merely predict the next screen action. However, much of the current mobile-agent literature still evaluates agents primarily as GUI controllers that observe a screen, emit taps and swipes, and are scored by target app state. Real phone-use tasks are broader: they require deciding when to use app GUIs, device-side commands, or structured tools, while leaving evidence that the intended side effect actually occurred. We introduce PhoneHarness, a mixed-action benchmark and execution harness for studying phone-use agents on verifiable mobile workflows. PhoneHarness runs a device-side agent loop over GUI, CLI, and host-side tool actions, combining deterministic action routing with bounded GUI delegation and auditable execution traces. Its benchmark, PhoneHarness Bench, evaluates whether agents complete tasks with observable side effects, not only whether they produce plausible final answers. On the annotated evaluation split, PhoneHarness reaches a 75.0% pass rate, outperforming the strongest non-PhoneHarness settings by 12.9 percentage points. PhoneHarness and PhoneHarness Bench therefore play distinct but mutually dependent roles: the harness makes mixed phone workflows executable, while the benchmark measures whether agents can use that harness reliably and safely. Our findings suggest that reliable phone automation depends on action-surface routing and verifiable execution, not only visual GUI control.",
      "abstract_zh": "当前手机智能体需要完成真实移动工作流，而非仅预测下一步屏幕动作，但现有研究大多仅将智能体作为GUI控制器评估，仅按目标应用状态评分。真实手机任务需要选择GUI、设备命令或结构化工具，并验证预期副作用。本文提出PhoneHarness，即面向可验证移动工作流的混合动作基准与执行框架，支持混合动作的设备端智能体循环，带可审计执行轨迹，在标注测试集上通过率达75.0%，比非PhoneHarness方案高12.9个百分点。",
      "has_code": false,
      "repo_url": "",
      "repo_stars": 0,
      "hf_upvotes": 0,
      "citation_count": 0,
      "venue": "",
      "venue_year": "",
      "venue_type": "",
      "venue_url": "",
      "venue_confidence": "",
      "venue_source": "",
      "is_authority_venue": false,
      "ingest_source": "",
      "manual_reason": "",
      "manual_tags": [],
      "problem": "现有移动智能体仅关注GUI控制，无法处理含混合动作、需验证副作用的真实手机任务，缺乏对应执行与评测框架。",
      "method": "提出PhoneHarness混合动作执行框架与评测基准，支持GUI、CLI、工具混合动作的设备端智能体循环，带可审计执行轨迹。",
      "contribution": "推出PhoneHarness执行框架与PhoneHarness Bench基准，在标注评测集上实现75.0%通过率，优于现有方案12.9个百分点。",
      "limitations": "摘要未提及",
      "key_finding": "可靠的手机自动化依赖动作面路由和可验证执行，而非仅视觉GUI控制，PhoneHarness通过率达75%，超基线12.9个百分点。",
      "theme": "手机智能体执行框架",
      "method_family": "agent harness",
      "agent_setting": "mobile/tool-use",
      "control_mechanism": "通过构建PhoneHarness执行框架，结合确定性动作路由、受限GUI委托与可审计轨迹，实现混合动作的可验证执行。",
      "evaluation_environment": "PhoneHarness Bench、标注移动工作流、任务通过率",
      "evaluation_signal": "PhoneHarness在标注评测分割集取得75.0%的任务通过率，比最强非PhoneHarness设置高出12.9个百分点，验证了方法有效性。",
      "failure_mode": "现有移动智能体仅关注GUI控制，无法完成需混合动作、可验证副作用的真实手机任务",
      "reliability_risk": "依赖真实移动设备执行，不同机型的环境差异可能影响结果复现，缺乏跨设备泛化性验证。",
      "industrial_relevance": "high",
