      "published": "",
      "collected": "2026-06-27",
      "abstract": "Significance Many applications of AI agents tacitly assume that, under uncertainty, they will react in roughly human-like ways, if not more rationally. Using a benchmark designed to elicit human choice strategies, we show this assumption often fails. Rather, LLM-powered agents are typically much more sensitive to ordinary choice architecture cues. Because some are helpful and others are not, this can push model decisions toward higher or lower payoffs. This complements prior work on prompt robustness and adversarial attacks, because it is triggered by benign, semantically meaningful features of the decision environment. While frontier reasoning models partially mitigate these effects, this comes at a substantial cost. Our findings identify behavioral robustness as a fundamental challenge for safe and trustworthy AI agents.",
      "abstract_zh": "许多AI智能体应用默认其在不确定性环境下的反应会近似人类甚至更为理性。本文通过针对人类选择策略设计的基准测试发现该假设通常不成立，大语言模型驱动的智能体对普通选择架构线索更敏感，良性环境特征也会改变决策收益，前沿模型仅能部分缓解该问题且成本高昂，本文指出行为鲁棒性是安全可信AI智能体的核心挑战。",
