      "id": "2606.27350",
      "direction_id": "agent-skills-harness",
      "direction_name": "Agent Skills 与 Harness",
      "week": "2026-W27",
      "title": "CHIA: An open-source framework for principled, agentic AI-driven hardware/software co-design research",
      "title_zh": "CHIA：面向原则性智能体驱动软硬件协同设计研究的开源框架",
      "authors": [
        "Angela Cui",
        "Ferran Hermida-Rivera",
        "Jack Toubes",
        "Raghav Gupta",
        "Jim Fang",
        "C. Zhang",
        "Ella Schwarz",
        "Junha Kim",
        "Yakun Sophia Shao",
        "Borivoje Nikolić",
        "Christopher W. Fletcher",
        "S. Karandikar"
      ],
      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2606.27350",
      "pdf_url": "http://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.27350",
      "category": "via-citation",
      "published": "",
      "collected": "2026-06-29",
      "abstract": "Agentic artificial intelligence shows great promise for radically improving the pace of innovation in hardware/software co-design research across computer architecture, systems, compilers, and VLSI. Thus far, however, applications of AI in these contexts have generally been demonstrated in isolated settings on small-scale problems, due to the difficulty of designing and deploying complex AI-infused hardware and software development workflows. This paper introduces CHIA, an open-source hardware/software co-design framework for agile and principled research on the application of AI to co-design. CHIA treats the productive construction and scalable deployment of the co-design flow itself as a first-class objective. In CHIA, agentic AI-driven hardware and software design flows are expressed as \\textit{CHIA loops}: directed cyclic graphs whose nodes execute various system-on-chip design tools, microarchitectural simulators, software build systems, AI models, evolutionary coding agents, and more. The \\textit{CHIA library} provides node implementations for many popular tools, including Chipyard, gem5, ChampSim, FireSim, Hammer (thus several commercial ASIC CAD tools), Vivado, AlphaEvolve, AdaEvolve, and many others. CHIA also provides a broad set of features to conduct principled science around these flows. These include isolation between AI models and hardware tools, profiling mechanisms, fault-tolerant execution, and reliability at scale across hundreds of heterogeneous systems (CPUs, FPGAs, GPUs, etc., across public cloud/on-prem.). To showcase CHIA, we present five CHIA loops as case studies: (1) automatic RTL-to-gem5 simulator alignment, (2) LLM-driven implementation of microarchitectural features in RTL, (3) agentic, IPC-aware critical path optimization, (4) evolutionary architectural discovery, and (5) maintainer-friendly agentic GitHub issue fixing.",
      "abstract_zh": "智能体AI有望大幅提升软硬件协同设计领域的创新速度，但目前这类AI应用大多只能在孤立环境解决小规模问题，难以部署复杂的AI融合开发工作流。本文推出开源框架CHIA，将协同设计流的构建部署作为核心目标，以有向循环图表达设计流，集成多类常用工具，提供隔离、 profiling、容错等特性，并用五个案例验证框架能力。",
      "has_code": false,
      "repo_url": "",
