      "id": "2607.14336",
      "direction_id": "agent-skills-harness",
      "direction_name": "Agent Skills 与 Harness",
      "week": "2026-W29",
      "title": "Copy-on-Write Scoring: Application-Specific Agent Evaluations",
      "title_zh": "写时复制评分：面向特定应用的智能体评估",
      "authors": [
        "Joanna Roy",
        "Sven Hoelzel"
      ],
      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2607.14336v1",
      "pdf_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2607.14336v1",
      "category": "cs.SE",
      "published": "2026-07-15 19:59:33+00:00",
      "collected": "2026-07-17",
      "abstract": "Trustworthy deployment of LLM-based agents in software systems requires evaluating how they perform on application-specific workflows, with enough granularity to localize where they succeed and fail. Yet existing agent evaluation mechanisms are limited: benchmarks have low construct validity for application-specific workflows and environments, and replica evaluation environments are expensive and prone to drift. We propose Copy-on-Write (CoW) Scoring, a framework that evaluates agent operations directly within application environments using a PostgreSQL-level Copy-on-Write mechanism to isolate agent writes. CoW Scoring produces session- and operation-level scores that highlight where agents' database write operations succeed and fail in a given application environment, enabling inexpensive evaluation and iteration on agent harnesses and tool surfaces. We demonstrate the framework on Plane, an open-source project-management platform, where analysis surfaced specific issues in the tool surface, and corresponding fixes produced measurable improvements on affected models.   Python library: https://github.com/trail-ml/agent-cow-python",
      "abstract_zh": "基于大语言模型的智能体要在软件系统中可信部署，需要针对特定应用工作流开展足够细粒度的评估，定位成败位置。但现有智能体评估机制存在局限：基准对特定应用工作流的结构效度低，复现评估环境成本高且易发生漂移。本文提出写时复制（CoW）评分框架，利用PostgreSQL级写时复制机制隔离智能体写入，可生成会话与操作级评估得分，支持低成本迭代智能体harness与工具面，已在开源项目管理平台Plane验证，修复问题后性能获得可测提升。",
      "has_code": true,
      "repo_url": "https://github.com/trail-ml/agent-cow-python",
      "repo_stars": 10,
      "hf_upvotes": 0,
      "citation_count": 0,
