      "title": "EvoRL: Evolution of Agentic Workflows Using Reinforcement Learning",
      "title_zh": "EvoRL：基于强化学习的智能体工作流演化方法",
      "authors": [
        "D. Attota",
        "Yingsha Xie"
      ],
      "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/d391fb34f9d44d55abbd0733cfc24d7d95932e33",
      "pdf_url": "",
      "category": "via-citation",
      "published": "",
      "collected": "2026-06-08",
      "abstract": "Recent advances in Large Language Models (LLMs) have enabled multi-agent systems capable of tackling complex tasks. Nevertheless, the performance of these systems is often limited by rigid, manually crafted “agentic workflows” that govern agent interactions. Such workflows are either too simplistic to handle complex problems or unnecessarily complex for simpler tasks, resulting in high computational costs and latency. To address these limitations, we introduce EvoRL, a novel framework that leverages hierarchical reinforcement learning to automate the construction of agentic workflows. EvoRL frames workflow design as a sequential decision-making process, learning adaptive policies to dynamically assemble workflows tailored to each query. The framework employs a high-level Evolver agent to select modular agentic components that define the workflow structure, and a low-level LLM Selector agent to choose the most cost-effective language model for each component. Empirical validation of EvoRL on benchmarks including GSM8K, MATH, MultiArith, HumanEval, and MBPP demonstrates that EvoRL achieves up to 87.99 % average accuracy, surpassing static baselines such as Chain-of-Thought (CoT) at $\\text{8 0. 4 5} \\%$ as well as stochastic methods. In addition, EvoRL reduces the average number of episodes required to reach a solution by 38% and substantially lowers computational costs. These findings highlight EvoRL's robust generalization across both mathematical reasoning and code generation domains.",
      "abstract_zh": "大语言模型进步让多智能体系统可处理复杂任务，但现有系统受限于人工设计的刚性智能体工作流，工作流要么过简单无法处理复杂问题，要么对简单任务冗余，导致计算成本高、延迟大。本文提出EvoRL框架，采用分层强化学习自动构建自适应工作流，两层智能体分别选择组件与匹配大模型，在多个基准上性能超越基线、降低成本。",
