      "title": "Mind Duel: Offline AI for Structured Debates",
      "title_zh": "《心智对决：面向结构化辩论的离线人工智能》",
      "authors": [
        "R. Patil",
        "Om Karmuse",
        "Shivanjali Belge",
        "Kundan Dhage",
        "Faraz Ansari"
      ],
      "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/08eb91a525dfe02df7c085c7be5febecdf54ca6b",
      "pdf_url": "",
      "category": "via-citation",
      "published": "",
      "collected": "2026-06-13",
      "abstract": "In this paper, we introduce AI Debater - an interactive chatbot hosted locally that is intended to engage in debates on issues specified by the user. The architecture is based on the DeepSeek-R1 14B large language model, which runs with the Ollama framework. Since all computations are carried out offline, privacy for the data is assured as well as latency is extremely low. Users can choose a personal tone for the debate level and degree of creativity for each AI speaker so that the tool can be used for learning, argumentation practice, or enjoyment. Streamlit is the framework employed to create the application's UI so that it is interactive and responsive. The design of the prompt guarantees the arguments advanced in debates are coherent, rational, and engaging. This paper illustrates the potential of instruction-conditioned language models for dialog systems as it opens up the possibility to AI-assisted tools for powerful reasoning and eloquent speech that will boost further development in this area.",
      "abstract_zh": "本文提出了本地部署的交互式辩论AI机器人AI Debater，基于DeepSeek-R1 14B大语言模型，通过Ollama框架离线运行，可保障隐私且延迟极低。用户可为每个AI辩手定制语气与创意程度，支持学习、辩论练习或娱乐场景，采用Streamlit搭建交互式UI，prompt设计保障辩论论点连贯理性有吸引力，展示了指令大模型在对话系统的应用潜力。",
