      "id": "2606.15874",
      "direction_id": "multi-agent-consistency",
      "direction_name": "多 Agent 交互与一致性",
      "week": "2026-W25",
      "title": "LLM-as-Code Agentic Programming for Agent Harness",
      "title_zh": "面向智能体管控的LLM即代码智能体编程",
      "authors": [
        "Junjia Qi",
        "Zichuan Fu",
        "Jingtong Gao",
        "Wenlin Zhang",
        "Hanyu Yan",
        "Xian Wu",
        "Xiangyu Zhao"
      ],
      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2606.15874v1",
      "pdf_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.15874v1",
      "category": "cs.AI",
      "published": "2026-06-14 15:47:27+00:00",
      "collected": "2026-06-16",
      "abstract": "Every major LLM agent framework gives the LLM the role of orchestrator; the model decides what to do next, when to call tools, and when to stop. We argue that token explosion, control-flow hallucination, and unreliable completion are not implementation bugs but architectural consequences of assigning the deterministic work of looping, branching, and sequencing to a probabilistic system. A better prompt or a stronger model cannot guarantee the reliability of the LLM agent. We therefore propose Agentic Programming, in which the program governs all control flow, and the LLM is itself part of it, an adaptive component we call LLM-as-Code and invoke only where a task calls for reasoning or generation. Within each call the model keeps full flexibility, but it cannot alter the program's execution path. With control in the program, the LLM's context is built from the execution history's call tree and forms a directed acyclic graph (DAG). Each call's context length is then determined by its call depth rather than by accumulation over steps. A case study of computer-use agents shows that the design is practical, not just a theoretical stance, substantially improving the stability of long visual operation sequences.",
      "abstract_zh": "现有主流大语言模型智能体框架均让LLM担任编排器，本文提出token爆炸、控制流幻觉等问题并非实现bug，而是将确定性控制流交给概率系统的架构缺陷，更好提示或更强模型都无法保证可靠性。因此提出智能体编程，由程序掌控所有控制流，LLM仅作为自适应组件按需调用，上下文按调用树DAG组织，避免长度累积，案例验证该设计可提升长序列稳定性。",
      "has_code": false,
      "repo_url": "",
      "repo_stars": 0,
      "hf_upvotes": 0,
      "citation_count": 0,
      "venue": "",
      "venue_year": "",
      "venue_type": "",
      "venue_url": "",
      "venue_confidence": "",
      "venue_source": "",
      "is_authority_venue": false,
      "ingest_source": "",
      "manual_reason": "",
      "manual_tags": [],
      "problem": "现有LLM智能体将循环、分支等确定性控制流交给概率大模型，引发token爆炸、控制流幻觉与可靠性不足问题。",
      "method": "提出智能体编程架构，由程序掌控全部控制流，LLM作为自适应组件仅按需调用，上下文按调用树DAG组织限制长度累积。",
      "contribution": "提出新的LLM智能体架构，解决长任务上下文长度累积问题，实证显示可显著提升长操作序列稳定性。",
      "limitations": "摘要未提及",
      "key_finding": "将确定性控制流交给概率LLM会天然引发token爆炸等问题，属于架构缺陷而非实现bug，程序控流可大幅提升长序列稳定性。",
      "theme": "智能体管控架构",
      "method_family": "agent harness",
      "agent_setting": "计算机使用/tool-use",
      "control_mechanism": "通过将循环分支等控制流交由确定性程序管控，仅推理生成时调用LLM，基于调用树DAG组织上下文避免长度累积。",
      "evaluation_environment": "计算机使用智能体长视觉操作序列任务",
      "evaluation_signal": "该架构可显著提升长视觉操作序列的运行稳定性，有效缓解原架构的上下文爆炸问题。",
      "failure_mode": "token爆炸、控制流幻觉、长序列运行不稳定",
      "reliability_risk": "仅开展了小范围案例研究，缺乏大规模多场景验证，架构通用性尚未得到充分证明。",
      "industrial_relevance": "high",
      "read_priority": "medium",
