      "title": "Differentiated Effects of Agent Diversity on Collective Decision-Making in LLM-Based Multi-Agent Delphi Systems",
      "title_zh": "智能体多样性对基于LLM的多智能体德尔菲系统集体决策的异质性影响",
      "authors": [
        "Namyeon Lee",
        "O. Kwon"
      ],
      "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/b9b2e3fd45eb39551947f9c7dedc41080f845262",
      "pdf_url": "",
      "category": "via-citation",
      "published": "",
      "collected": "2026-07-16",
      "abstract": "Large language model (LLM)-based multi-agent systems are increasingly being explored as tools for supporting structured collective decision-making, but it remains unclear how the diversity structure of agent groups affects decision-making performance. This study examined the effects of agent diversity in a Delphi-based multi-agent system by applying Harrison and Klein’s framework of variety, separation, and disparity. An LLM-based Multi-Agent Delphi System (MADS) was implemented, and 11 agent-group conditions were constructed by manipulating personality-based variety, belief-orientation-based separation, and influence asymmetry. Each condition consisted of eight agents and was tested across four open-weight LLMs with repeated experimental runs. Performance was evaluated in terms of idea exploration extent, consensus quality, and consensus efficiency, using a human expert Delphi study as an external benchmark. The results showed that diversity had differentiated effects across performance dimensions. The maximum diversity group achieved the highest idea exploration but showed low consensus quality and efficiency, whereas the homogeneous group achieved stable consensus quality and efficiency but limited exploration. The separation diversity conditions formed Pareto-efficient alternatives, indicating balanced trade-offs between idea exploration and consensus. These findings indicate that agent diversity does not uniformly improve collective decision-making performance; instead, its appropriate structure depends on whether the task prioritizes exploration, consensus quality, or consensus efficiency.",
      "abstract_zh": "基于大语言模型（LLM）的多智能体系统越来越多地被用于支持结构化集体决策，但智能体群体的多样性结构如何影响决策性能仍不明确。本研究基于经典多样性框架，构建了基于LLM的多智能体德尔菲系统，设置11种不同多样性条件，在4种开放权重LLM上开展重复实验，以人类专家德尔菲研究为基准评估性能。",
