      "id": "2607.09748",
      "direction_id": "multi-agent-consistency",
      "direction_name": "多 Agent 交互与一致性",
      "week": "2026-W29",
      "title": "Replicating Belief, Not Bits: Epistemic State Replication for Agentic Systems",
      "title_zh": "复制信念而非比特：面向智能体系统的认知状态复制",
      "authors": [
        "Junfei He",
        "Deying Yu"
      ],
      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2607.09748",
      "pdf_url": "http://arxiv.org/pdf/2607.09748",
      "category": "via-citation",
      "published": "",
      "collected": "2026-07-17",
      "abstract": "In distributed systems, the classical State Machine Replication (SMR) model assumes that correct replicas execute deterministic transitions to yield identical bitwise states. However, the rise of agentic distributed systems -- where autonomous, stochastic, and model-driven agents orchestrate infrastructure -- presents scenarios where deterministic, bitwise replication is insufficient. Replicas operating with generative models may exhibit divergent reasoning paths, summaries, and token boundaries, yet reach semantically equivalent and correct operational decisions. Forcing bitwise agreement across these stochastic participants degrades execution flexibility, induces context amnesia, and limits performance. We argue that in such settings replicas should agree on belief, not bits. We propose Epistemic State Replication (ESR), a belief-replication layer for agentic distributed systems that shifts the replication boundary from data visibility to knowledge visibility. We formalize the epistemic node state as a pair K = (L, B) separating the deterministic, immutable evidence log (L) from the stochastic, evolving belief lineage (B). To govern execution safety, we define Semantic Linearizability, which requires operations to reflect the latest committed operational meaning within a verifier-bounded semantic compatibility metric, and Bounded Eventual Coherence, which bounds expected semantic divergence under fair delivery, monotonic evidence, bounded verifier disturbance, and a contractive graft operator. We outline protocols for propagating derived insights using structured epistemic deltas, and formalize Verifiable Semantic Rollbacks to prune faulty premises from belief lineages without inducing context amnesia. We prototype ESR and report preliminary simulation results that show feasibility under the stated assumptions and illustrate reductions in secondary cognitive faults.",
      "abstract_zh": "分布式系统经典状态机复制（SMR）要求副本得到比特级一致状态，但自主随机的模型驱动智能体常出现推理路径不同但语义决策等价的情况，强制比特一致会降低灵活性、引发上下文遗忘、限制性能。本文提出认知状态复制ESR，将复制边界转为知识可见性，定义一致性保障，给出协议与回滚机制，原型验证了方法可行性，可减少次级认知故障。",
      "has_code": false,
      "repo_url": "",
      "repo_stars": 0,
      "hf_upvotes": 0,
      "citation_count": 0,
      "venue": "",
      "venue_year": "",
      "venue_type": "",
      "venue_url": "",
      "venue_confidence": "",
      "venue_source": "",
      "is_authority_venue": false,
      "ingest_source": "",
      "manual_reason": "",
      "manual_tags": [],
      "problem": "传统比特级状态复制无法适配随机智能体分布式系统，强制比特一致会降低灵活性，引发多种认知故障。",
      "method": "提出认知状态复制ESR，将复制边界从数据可见性转为知识可见性，分离证据与信念，定义语义一致性保障。",
      "contribution": "提出信念复制而非比特复制的思路，设计ESR框架，初步验证方法可行，可减少智能体系统次级认知故障。",
      "limitations": "摘要未提及",
      "key_finding": "随机智能体分布式系统中，复制信念而非比特满足一致性要求，还可有效减少系统的次级认知故障。",
      "theme": "多Agent一致性",
      "method_family": "multi-agent coordination",
      "agent_setting": "多智能体分布式系统",
      "control_mechanism": "设计信念复制层，分离证据与信念，基于验证器约束语义一致性，通过可验证回滚剪枝错误前提。",
