      "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/b09ce135b991d34ff5e0a61168fa8d9e040461b4",
      "pdf_url": "",
      "category": "via-citation",
      "published": "",
      "collected": "2026-07-16",
      "abstract": "Web agents built on large language models (LLMs) show strong potential for automating multi-step interactions on real-world webpages, yet their performance is fundamentally limited by the quality of training data. Human demonstrations are costly to obtain, while LLM-generated trajectories are abundant but noisy and inconsistent, making them unsuitable as direct supervision. We propose Multi-Trajectory Consensus Self-Distillation (MT-CSD), a framework that enables reliable, annotation-free improvement of web agents. MT-CSD transforms diverse rollout trajectories into stable pseudo-demonstrations by aligning their structural patterns, aggregating consistent action and rationale signals across trajectories, and distilling the resulting consensus back into the model. Through cross-trajectory evidence consolidation, MT-CSD mitigates error propagation and yields substantially more robust supervision than single-rollout self-training approaches. Experiments on the WebShop benchmark demonstrate that MT-CSD consistently improves success rate and step efficiency than other baselines, highlighting consensus-driven self-distillation as an effective direction for scalable web agent training.",
      "abstract_zh": "基于大语言模型构建的Web智能体可自动化真实网页的多步交互，性能却受训练数据质量限制：人工演示获取成本高，大模型生成轨迹丰富但存在噪声、不一致，无法直接用作监督。本文提出无标注的多轨迹共识自蒸馏框架MT-CSD，通过跨轨迹整合缓解误差传播，在WebShop基准上效果优于基线。",
